node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store
.tade-test-*/
# Tade writes its own bookkeeping under .tade/ — task files, the context an
# agent was handed, pasted attachments, check runs, locks — and none of it is
# this project's: it is one machine's and one person's, and it was being
# committed. There is no exception any more: `checks.yaml` used to be one,
# because CI was generated from it, and now nothing is — what this project
# checks is read out of .github/workflows/ci.yml and .githooks/pre-commit,
# which are the files that were always going to be the truth about it.
#
# `/.tade/*` and not `/.tade/`, which now say the same thing: it is the
# contents because there used to be an exception under them, and it stays the
# contents because that is the line already in every repository Tade has
# worked in.
#
# One of these earns its own note. `checks.running.json` says what is being
# checked right now and is taken back when the run ends, and while it is there
# `pnpm exec biome ci .` read it as a file somebody had written badly — which
# made `format` fail inside every run that wrote it.
/.tade/*
